  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/turning/offset.rs`: a new private step `thin` runs after the bisection in `profile_offset` and `profile_offset_in`.\n- `thin` drops each sample that is closer than half the chord share (`MIN_GAP_SHARE = 0.5`) to the last kept sample.\n- The first and the last sample (the window ends) always stay. At the end, a kept sample that is too near the last sample gives way to it.\n- Each kept sample is an exact point of the offset curve. No new point is made.\n- A chord moves by at most two gaps (one share). The callers pass a quarter of the user tolerance as the share, so the ride stays within half of the user tolerance.\n- The module doc now states this bound.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe bisection (`settle`) halves the interval toward a vertical tangent of the offset curve. The samples come closer than 1 micrometre. Exact float twins of candidate stations also occur (a gap of 1e-16 mm). `out.dedup()` removes only exactly equal samples. The lathe posts wrote these runs as identical `G01` blocks.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew file `crates/motion/tests/turning_offset_spacing.rs`:\n\n- `od_ride_has_no_move_shorter_than_half_the_share`: the stepped bar and the collar, tol 1e-2, 2.5e-3 and 1e-4.\n- `id_ride_has_no_move_shorter_than_half_the_share`: the stepped hole wall.\n- `a_window_end_next_to_a_candidate_keeps_the_gap`: the window ends 1e-7 past a candidate station. This pins the give-way at the end.\n- `thinning_keeps_the_window_ends_and_the_nose`: the ends stay, and each sample is at distance d from the profile.\n- `thinned_chords_stay_within_the_bound`: 9 points on each chord stand at least `d - 2 * tol` from the profile.\n\nRed before the fix: yes. On unchanged `offset.rs` the OD and ID spacing pins fail with `gap 0.00000000000000044` (OD) and `gap 0.00000000000000011` (ID).\n\nMutations:\n\n- The old `offset.rs`: 2 pins red. Restored: green.\n- The tail give-way disabled (`while ... && false`): `a_window_end_next_to_a_candidate_keeps_the_gap` red (`gap 0.0000001`). Restored: green.\n\nLatest review fix (final head `a8dc06bd903d41af16461ebb15e7827a747f3b4a`):\n\n- The branch merges `upstream/main` at `fc32feb0e`. The merge is clean.\n- This includes the reviewed fix for #3050, PR #3078 (merge `eefee2453e`).\n- The Linux bore count pin is `(3158, 3130, 1141)`. The verification checks stay in place.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --case turning/contour-finishes` rebuilds the project and the NC file.\n- Both catalog regeneration paths pin the refreshed NC bytes.\n- Artifact review: the NC file goes from 620 to 246 lines. The diff removes 388 lines and adds 14 lines.\n  - 374 short `G01` blocks are removed.\n  - 13 `G00` blocks and one `G01` retract change X from `20.762` to `20.76`, or from `22.884` to `22.88`.\n  - The other command types and feed rates stay the same.\n  - The project changes two operation stamps and two cached move lists (60 to 16, and 536 to 206).\n  - The parameters, model, machine, and setup stay the same.\n- Catalog mutation: with the old NC file, both `catalog_turning_contour_finishes::regenerates` and `catalog_turning_contour_finishes::rebuilds` fail. With the refreshed NC file, both pass.\n- Bore pin mutation: with the old Linux helper counts, `the_linux_x86_64_bore_count_pin_is_exact` fails. With the current helper restored, it passes.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog`: 33 passed, 0 failed, 2 ignored.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 655 steps, 0 failed, 37.4 min.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: green, 234 steps, 0 failed, 41.3 min. All reached lanes ran, with no omissions.\n  - The 234 steps include one release build and 233 test lanes. All gate steps are green.\n  - Motion heavy lanes: 37 lanes; 57 ordinary tests pass. Two known-fail lanes for #1950 are red as expected.\n  - App heavy lanes: 196 lanes; 43 ordinary tests pass. Four known-fail lanes are red as expected: one for #1950 and three for #2849.\n  - `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm` passes, including `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green, exit 0, 38.1 s (`--all-targets -- -D warnings`).\n\n## Catalog example\n\n`examples/catalog/turning/cone-thread` came to main after this branch was made. The branch merges main and rebuilds the case with `cargo xtask catalog --case turning/cone-thread`.\n\n- `cone-thread.nc`: 1197 lines to 732 lines. 465 `G01` lines are removed and 0 lines are added. The runs of same-X `G01` blocks go from 509 to 82.\n- `cone-thread.camproj`: rebuilt with the new ride samples.\n- `README.md`: the limit line for #2882 (repeated blocks) is removed. The taper blocks and the thread blocks that the README names stay the same.\n- Mutation: with the old `.nc` back, `catalog_turning_cone_thread::regenerates` and `catalog_turning_cone_thread::rebuilds` are red. With the new `.nc`, they are green.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n4 files. Each diff only removes lines (516 removed, 0 added):\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/profile_rough_finish.nc` (-129)\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/inch/fanuc-lathe/profile_rough_finish.nc` (-129)\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach-lathe/turning_mm.nc` (-129)\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach-lathe/turning_inch.nc` (-129)\n\nMost removed lines are runs of identical blocks, for example 40 x `G01 X7. Z2. F0.04` and 39 x `G01 X9.1 Z3.05 F0.05`. The other removed lines are sub-gap steps at the start of the same face, for example `Z2.001` to `Z2.005`. The goldens were made again with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- At a very small user tolerance (for example 0.001 mm) the gap is less than the posted resolution. Two rounded blocks can then still be equal. This costs no position.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `offset.rs` or the new test file.\n\n## Decision\n\n`docs/decisions/2882-ride-min-spacing.md`. The post-side alternative (drop a repeated block in each lathe post) was dropped.\n\nWritten by an Opus lead + Haiku workers (lane trial). The workers wrote about 85% of the lines: `thin` and its call sites, the first four pins, and the decision record. The lead wrote about 15%: the chord-bound correction (1.5x to 2x share, because the give-way at the end can double the gap), the tail pin, the clippy fix, the golden refresh and the review.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Turning profile rides no longer post runs of identical G01 blocks: samples closer than half the chord share are dropped.\n\nFixes #2882\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
